The final phase is the presentation and demonstration of the completed project.

Main activities:

* Introduce the project.
* Explain the problem and objectives.
* Explain the technologies used.
* Demonstrate the main features.
* Show the project working in real time.
* Explain the results.
* Answer questions from teachers/examiners.

Example: During the college project viva, students demonstrate the attendance system by logging in, marking attendance, and showing the generated report.
